  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Sets: membership and counting</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core and Essential 1.1 (a): Decide whether statements using the symbols for is an element of, is not an element of, and n(A) are true for a described set.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 11, Exercise A, question 8 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 3 (Metric), ed. A. G. Howson, Cambridge University Press, 1967: deciding whether a number is or is not a member of a set; every set is new, in a true-or-false form with a count.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
